qwen3-tts: Qwen3-TTS-12Hz-1.7B-CustomVoice text-to-speech on the NPU

Runs the Qwen3-TTS talker and code predictor on the prebuilt qwen3_npu engine
(stock Qwen3 Q4NX packages with injected input embeddings and an identity
lm_head; decode steps replay engine-built runlists, no per-step rebuild) and
everything else on the CPU (embeddings, heads, sampling, 24 kHz speech decoder).

- src/{include,common}/qwen3_tts: engine, load-time XRT capture (only the
  interposed symbols are exported, and they only record while a TTS engine is
  being constructed), text segmentation, garble detector with opportunistic
  retry, loudness matching, kernel-log NPU fault watchdog.
- server: POST /v1/audio/speech (OpenAI / vLLM-Omni shape; WAV/PCM, whole or
  streamed), GET /v1/audio/speech/stream (WebSocket, text in as produced),
  /v1/audio/voices, /v1/audio/speech/cancel; raw-response, WebSocket-upgrade
  and admission hooks in WebServer.
- flm run <tts model> speaks text to WAV; flm serve <tts model> or
  --tts <tag>; model_list entry qwen3-tts:1.7b (built locally, not downloaded;
  flm pull explains how).
- Linux + XRT only (compiled out on Windows and HRX builds).
- test/qwen3_tts: CPU-only segmentation tests.

The model package is built with the tools in the qwen3-tts-package-tools patch.

